%% alt: Internal teams call through the AI gateway, which handles auth, quotas and telemetry, to an inference router that is queue-, cache- and prefix-aware. The router sends interactive and bulk traffic to separate pools of engine replicas, which load signed model weights from object storage. An autoscaler sizes both pools on queue depth and KV-cache use, and the pools report TTFT, TPOT, queue and cache metrics.
flowchart TB
  T[Teams]:::human --> GW[AI gateway<br/>auth, quotas, telemetry]:::control
  GW --> IG[Inference router<br/>queue-, cache- and prefix-aware]:::control
  IG --> P1[Interactive pool<br/>engine replicas]:::model
  IG --> P2[Bulk pool<br/>engine replicas]:::model
  AS[Autoscaler<br/>queue depth, KV-cache use]:::tool -.-> P1 & P2
  W[(Signed model weights<br/>object storage)]:::data --> P1 & P2
  P1 & P2 --> M[(Metrics: TTFT, TPOT,<br/>queue, cache use)]:::data
